#N canvas 20 20 2000 1400 12;
#X text 20 20 m_nanokey -- the Korg nanoKEY's input layer: its keys \, from any channel of its port \, out a cord as <note> <velocity> \, 0 for a release. It knows nothing about which synth a key plays: c_synth decides that. ref/device/nanokey.md, f 70;
#X text 20 150 creation arg 1: the first Pd channel of the nanoKEY's port \, 49 on the device: Midi-In 4 \, which it shares with the Volca interface's DIN IN \, where nothing arrives. inlets: none. outlet 1: <note> <velocity> \, to c_synth. On presence \, passive: expect at load \, and seen with every key it passes., f 70;
#X obj 20 400 notein;
#X obj 400 470 - \$1;
#X obj 400 520 t f f;
#X obj 400 570 >= 0;
#X obj 560 570 < 16;
#X obj 400 620 *;
#X obj 20 560 pack f f;
#X obj 20 640 spigot;
#X obj 20 800 outlet;
#X text 700 400 notein fires right to left: the channel opens or shuts the spigot \, the velocity lands in pack's cold inlet \, then the note sends the pair. Any channel of the port \, 0 <= channel - block < 16 \, so a nanoKEY set to another channel still plays \, and the Launchpad \, the nano and the Streichfett \, on the ports below \, never do., f 50;
#X text 700 700 Passive on the presence roster \, as m_organelle is: it registers at load and says seen with every key it passes \, ahead of the key \, so g_oled's diag layer reads here once it has played \, and it is never polled and never ages. Polling is ruled out: its identity reply carries Korg's 42 \, the nanoKONTROL's byte \, so c_devid 66 would take it as the nano's (ref/device/nanokey.md \, ref/module/presence.md)., f 50;
#X obj 20 1000 loadbang;
#X obj 20 1050 del 2000;
#X obj 20 1100 f \$1;
#X obj 20 1150 print m_nanokey-channel;
#X text 300 1050 Prints the channel block it got \, since a wrong count of creation arguments loads in silence. C-9, f 50;
#X obj 20 720 t a b;
#X msg 200 760 seen m_nanokey;
#X obj 200 800 s presence;
#X obj 1100 1000 loadbang;
#X msg 1100 1050 expect m_nanokey passive;
#X obj 1100 1100 s presence;
